From 21cb61c4d936a849cc47fab8349ad594e3f6b220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:49:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: nvpair: keep the releng/15.1 XDR callback types

nvpair.c picks 2-argument xdrproc_t callbacks when
__FreeBSD_version >= 1600010 ("FreeBSD 16"). NextBSD's world is the
releng/15.1 tree, whose <rpc/xdr.h> still declares xdrproc_t as
bool_t (*)(XDR *, ...). Once NextBSD sets __FreeBSD_version to 2700000,
the 16.x branch is taken and buildworld fails with
-Wincompatible-function-pointer-types.

Drop the FreeBSD clause, so only the Linux kernel takes the 2-argument
branch and NextBSD keeps the variadic releng/15.1 callbacks. At 1501000
the clause is false, so nothing changes today.

Refs nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel#376. Carried out-of-tree for NextBSD.
---
 sys/contrib/openzfs/module/nvpair/nvpair.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/contrib/openzfs/module/nvpair/nvpair.c b/sys/contrib/openzfs/module/nvpair/nvpair.c
index 52678bb2b..7f392132f 100644
--- a/sys/contrib/openzfs/module/nvpair/nvpair.c
+++ b/sys/contrib/openzfs/module/nvpair/nvpair.c
@@ -3272,8 +3272,7 @@ nvs_xdr_nvl_fini(nvstream_t *nvs)
  * xdrproc_t-compatible callbacks for xdr_array()
  */
 
-#if (defined(__FreeBSD_version) && __FreeBSD_version >= 1600010) || \
-    defined(_KERNEL) && defined(__linux__) /* Linux kernel */
+#if defined(_KERNEL) && defined(__linux__) /* Linux kernel */
 
 #define	NVS_BUILD_XDRPROC_T(type)		\
 static bool_t					\
-- 
